 # Layout Patterns & Best Practices

## Grid-Flex Combo Pattern

This pattern combines CSS Grid for overall page structure with Flexbox for component-level layouts, providing both macro and micro-level control.

### Page Structure
```tsx
<div className="p-4">
  {/* Main grid container */}
  <div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-6">
    {/* Content sections */}
    <div className="col-span-3">
      <div className="flex flex-col gap-6">
        {/* Nested grid for cards */}
        <div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-6">
          {/* Individual cards */}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    {/* Sidebar section */}
    <div className="col-span-1">
      {/* Sidebar content */}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Key Principles

1. **Grid for Page Layout**
   - Use `grid-cols-4` as base layout
   - Common spans: `col-span-3` for main content, `col-span-1` for sidebar
   - Consistent gap spacing: `gap-6` for major sections

2. **Flex for Component Layout**
   - Use `flex flex-col` for vertical stacking
   - Use `flex items-center` for vertical alignment
   - Use `flex justify-between` for horizontal spacing
   - Use `gap-{size}` for consistent spacing

3. **Spacing Consistency**
   - Page padding: `p-4`
   - Major sections: `gap-6`
   - Component internal: `p-4` or `p-6`
   - Element spacing: `gap-2` or `gap-4`

4. **Responsive Patterns**
   ```tsx
   // Responsive grid
   <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
   
   // Responsive padding
   <div className="p-2 sm:p-4 lg:p-6">
   
   // Responsive spans
   <div className="col-span-4 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-1">
   ```

### Common Components

1. **Card Headers**
   ```tsx
   <div className="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
     <div className="space-y-1">
       <h3 className="font-semibold">{title}</h3>
       <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{subtitle}</p>
     </div>
     <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
       {/* Actions */}
     </div>
   </div>
   ```

2. **Data Lists**
   ```tsx
   <div className="space-y-4">
     {items.map((item) => (
       <div key={item.id} className="flex items-center gap-4">
         <div className="flex-1">
           <div className="font-medium">{item.title}</div>
           <div className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{item.subtitle}</div>
         </div>
         <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
           {/* Actions */}
         </div>
       </div>
     ))}
   </div>
   ```

3. **Stats Grid**
   ```tsx
   <div className="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
     {stats.map((stat) => (
       <div key={stat.id} className="p-4 rounded-lg bg-card">
         <div className="text-2xl font-semibold">{stat.value}</div>
         <div className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{stat.label}</div>
       </div>
     ))}
   </div>
   ```

### Best Practices

1. **Container Hierarchy**
   - Page Container → Grid Layout → Section Container → Component Container
   - Each level should handle its own spacing concerns
   - Use consistent class ordering: layout → spacing → typography → colors

2. **Responsive Design**
   - Start with mobile layout
   - Add breakpoints progressively
   - Use consistent breakpoint patterns across the app
   - Consider content rather than devices for breakpoints

3. **Component Composition**
   - Keep components focused and reusable
   - Use composition over configuration when possible
   - Maintain consistent spacing patterns
   - Use semantic HTML structure

4. **Performance Considerations**
   - Avoid deeply nested grids
   - Use CSS Grid for 2D layouts
   - Use Flexbox for 1D layouts
   - Consider content reflow during loading

Remember: This pattern provides a consistent and maintainable approach to layout that scales well with complexity while maintaining visual harmony across the application.